{"uid":"662533ac421a5f6b","name":"test_ordering_only_must_name_one_of_the_tasks_own_dependson_ids","fullName":"tests.test_plan_ingestion#test_ordering_only_must_name_one_of_the_tasks_own_dependson_ids","historyId":"7a453e23e5678440db97b6744b9213c3","time":{"start":1791930613874,"stop":1791930613875,"duration":1},"description":"GH #209 defect 3's residual: `orderingOnly` marks a SUBSET of the\n    edges a task actually has, so an entry that is not one of its own\n    `dependsOn` ids declares nothing and is refused rather than silently\n    ignored -- an inert declaration reads, to the planner that wrote it, as\n    an ordering edge the cure pass then drags back through anyway.\n\n    The SEMANTIC claim (that this dependency really produces none of the\n    evidence the task reports on) is deliberately NOT linted: it is the one\n    judgement the engine cannot make, which is why the field is declared by\n    the planner at all. `plan_ingestion.ordering_only_dependencies`' own\n    conservative default is what bounds a wrong declaration.","descriptionHtml":"<p>GH #209 defect 3's residual: <code>orderingOnly</code> marks a SUBSET of the<br />\nedges a task actually has, so an entry that is not one of its own<br />\n<code>dependsOn</code> ids declares nothing and is refused rather than silently<br />\nignored -- an inert declaration reads, to the planner that wrote it, as<br />\nan ordering edge the cure pass then drags back through anyway.</p>\n<pre><code>The SEMANTIC claim (that this dependency really produces none of the\nevidence the task reports on) is deliberately NOT linted: it is the one\njudgement the engine cannot make, which is why the field is declared by\nthe planner at all. `plan_ingestion.ordering_only_dependencies`' own\nconservative default is what bounds a wrong declaration.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_l